cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRAG in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PRAG: Paninian Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Safety-Critical Medical AI"
abstract: >
  PRAG is a governance-aware RAG architecture that applies a deterministic
  rule layer — inspired by Pāṇini's Ashtadhyayi conflict-resolution
  principles — between retrieval and generation. On 170 safety-critical
  medical questions, the rule engine fires 52.7% more than on general
  questions and blocks dangerous context at 111.6% higher rate. An
  ablation study across four modes provides causal proof that the
  Pāṇinian rule hierarchy itself contributes to safe answer generation,
  including a clinically critical eclampsia case where standard RAG
  recommended the wrong drug class and PRAG recommended the correct one.
